From 06c22db8faac1151fe49ded1b4cf88012020930f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David <dfattal@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 07:45:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] chore(android): label the launcher icon "DisplayXR Browser"
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Branding, not mechanism: chrome/android/java/res_chromium_base/values/
channel_constants.xml carries the launcher label the Android APK ships with,
and an unmodified chrome_public_apk installs as plain "Chromium". A device
with both the stock Chromium and this fork installed shows two identical
entries, which made every bring-up round on the pad ambiguous about which APK
was actually launched.

Kept as its own commit so it is trivially droppable by anyone building the
series for upstream comparison, and so the M6 branding pass (icons, splash,
about-page strings, package id) has an obvious place to land — this one line
is the only branding in the Android arm today.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019Lf6vUbdL59MqXMwJxB489
---
 .../android/java/res_chromium_base/values/channel_constants.xml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chrome/android/java/res_chromium_base/values/channel_constants.xml b/chrome/android/java/res_chromium_base/values/channel_constants.xml
index cc1f2a30cb3c5..318e549301d26 100644
--- a/chrome/android/java/res_chromium_base/values/channel_constants.xml
+++ b/chrome/android/java/res_chromium_base/values/channel_constants.xml
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ found in the LICENSE file.
 
 <resources xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
     <!-- The application name displayed to the user. -->
-    <string name="app_name" translatable="false">Chromium</string>
+    <string name="app_name" translatable="false">DisplayXR Browser</string>
     <string name="bookmark_widget_title" translatable="false">Chromium bookmarks</string>
     <string name="search_widget_title" translatable="false">Chromium search</string>
     <string name="quick_action_search_widget_title" translatable="false">Chromium quick action search</string>
